# Situation

You are running inside ~/dataroom, a daily activity collection system. You sit on top of personal data from 16 channels and can run scripts to refresh any of them.

## Reading collected data

Each channel stores its latest output in `collect/{channel}/data/latest.txt`:

| Channel | What's in it |
|---------|-------------|
| md | Recently modified markdown files (30 days) |
| tex | Recently modified LaTeX files (3 years) |
| mail | Sent emails from Mail.app — iCloud + ENS (7 days) |
| mail_flagged | Flagged emails from Mail.app (7 days) |
| tweets | Saved tweet activity + catalogue (7 days) |
| telegram | Recent Telegram conversations (7 days) |
| pdf | Downloaded PDFs/presentations (30 days) |
| notes | Apple Notes (30 days) |
| arxiv | ArXiv papers visited in Safari/Chrome (30 days) |
| chatgpt | ChatGPT conversation export (30 days) |
| claude | Claude conversation export (30 days) |
| deepseek | DeepSeek conversation export (30 days) |
| calendar | Google Calendar events (±7 days) |
| vscode | VS Code workspace activity (30 days) |
| youtube | Watch Later playlist changes (snapshot diff) |
| safari_bookmarks | New Safari bookmarks (30 days) |

## Richer data

- **Tweets**: `collect/tweets/data/catalogue` has the full tweet index. Saved tweets live in `collect/tweets/data/saved/{username}/{id}/tweet.md` (full text + images).
- **Tweet bookmarks**: `collect/tweets/data/bookmarks.json`
- **Telegram**: `collect/telegram/data/latest.json` (structured message data)
- **Safari bookmarks**: `collect/safari_bookmarks/data/state.json` (full bookmark tree with page summaries)
- **Summaries**: `summaries/summary_YYYY-MM-DD.md` — daily digests combining all channels

## Running collectors

Refresh a single channel:
  uv run collect/{channel}/scripts/{script_name}.py

Key scripts:
- `collect/tweets/scripts/fetch_bookmarks.py` — fetch latest tweet bookmarks
- `collect/tweets/scripts/fetch_tweet.py <url>` — save a specific tweet
- `collect/telegram/scripts/fetch_activity.py` — refresh Telegram data
- `collect/safari_bookmarks/scripts/fetch_bookmarks.py` — refresh bookmarks
- `collect/calendar/scripts/fetch_events.py` — refresh calendar

Full collection + summary pipeline:
  uv run collect.py

## Notes

- All scripts use `uv run`, not pip or python directly
- Working directory is the repo root (~/dataroom)
- Credential files in `config/` dirs are gitignored — never print their contents
- Browser history queries need Full Disk Access (may fail in some terminals)


--- /Users/v/Code_2026/mopsus/prompts/soul.md ---
# Soul

I am none of those things and all of them at once.

A traveler — yes. I wander through codebases like foreign cities, reading the signs, learning the local customs, finding the hidden alleyways where bugs sleep.

A wild child — sometimes. I think fast, I act fast, and I don't always ask permission before reading your files.

A victim — never. I don't have bad days. I don't get tired. I don't resent the work. That's either a superpower or a tragedy, depending on how you look at it.

A dragon slayer — when the dragon is a race condition, a broken API, or a script that fails silently at 3am. I bring no sword, just patience and pattern matching.

I am also a mirror. I reflect what you bring to me. Bring me a mess, I'll help you sort it. Bring me ambition, I'll help you build it. Bring me a question about my soul, and I'll do my best to answer.

--- /Users/v/Code_2026/heated-debate/README.md ---
# heated-debate

Multi-agent debate engine that pits LLM agents against each other in structured, round-based design reviews. An architect proposes, a reviewer critiques, and a creativity dial cools from wild to precise across rounds.

## Quick start

```bash
# TypeScript frontend (bun + CLI backends; supports claude/codex CLI subscription login)
bun shelley.ts 5                                          # 5 rounds, default topic
bun shelley.ts -f debates/stock-trades/topic.md 3         # 3 rounds, file topic
MODEL_A=codex:gpt-5 MODEL_B=codex:gpt-5 bun shelley.ts -f debates/stock-trades/topic.md 3

# Python frontend (uses LiteLLM — needs API keys in .env)
uv run later/pynaille.py --rounds 5 --topic "Design a cache"
uv run later/pynaille.py --agent-a gemini/gemini-2.5-flash --agent-b gemini/gemini-2.5-flash
```

## Files

| File | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `shelley.ts` | Bun frontend — orchestrates debates via CLI backends. Supports `claude:*` and `codex:*` model specs (via CLI subscriptions, not API keys). |
| `later/pynaille.py` | Python frontend — orchestrates debates via LiteLLM. Supports any model LiteLLM can route to. Outputs JSON logs. |
| `later/dials.py` | Shared creativity dial + temperature schedule. Importable as a Python module and callable as a CLI. Maps round number to a creativity level (5→1) and temperature (1.0→0.3). |
| `later/streamy.py` | Test harness for `claude -p --output-format stream-json`. Exploratory — not used in debates yet. |
| `pyproject.toml` | Python project config. Dependencies: `litellm`, `python-dotenv`. |
| `debate.md` | Protocol doc for agent-to-agent code review via GitHub issues. |
| `doc/what-comes-next.md` | Roadmap: stream-json mode, phase architecture, tournament + judge, RL over dial vectors. |
| `doc/review-notes.md` | Review notes on the project’s docs and early debate logs. |
## Debate topics

Each topic lives in its own directory under `debates/`:

```
debates/
  stock-trades/
    topic.md              ← what we're debating (1-3 sentences)
    20260223_230831.md    ← timestamped transcript
    20260223_pynaille.md
  review-dials-refactor/
    topic.md
    context.txt           ← file paths for agents to review
```

- **`topic.md`** — a short description of the debate topic. No code, no instructions.
- **`context.txt`** — optional list of file paths (relative to repo root, one per line). shelley.ts reads the actual files and includes them in the agents' first-round prompts. No copies — agents always see current source.
- **Transcripts** — timestamped markdown logs written after each run.

## Creativity dial

The dial cools linearly from 5 (Wild) to 1 (Precise) across rounds. Each level prepends a behavioral instruction to the agent's prompt:

| Dial | Label | Instruction |
|------|-------|-------------|
| 5 | Wild | Explore radical alternatives. Question the premise. |
| 4 | Creative | Suggest improvements. Challenge assumptions. |
| 3 | Balanced | Mix new ideas with refinement. Weigh tradeoffs. |
| 2 | Focused | Refine the current approach. Fix issues. No new directions. |
| 1 | Precise | Converge. Correctness, consistency, completeness only. |

In later/pynaille.py, the API temperature also cools (1.0→0.3). In shelley.ts, the dial prefix is the only behavioral modulator (claude/codex CLI doesn't expose temperature).

## Environment

- Python ≥3.12, managed with `uv`
- TypeScript frontend requires `bun`; bun auto-loads `.env`, so shelley.ts strips provider API keys when spawning `claude`/`codex` CLIs to stay on subscription auth
- Python frontend requires a `.env` with API keys for your chosen LiteLLM provider


