# Mopsus

Dual-agent Telegram bot (Claude + Codex) with data room integration. Mopsus connects to your local data room, lets you query it via Telegram, and runs an autonomous daily think phase that proposes ideas based on your activity.

## Architecture

![Architecture diagram](doc/mopsus_architecture.png)

Mopsus runs as a long-lived Telegram daemon with two AI backends (Claude CLI and Codex CLI). It maintains a **blackboard** — a persistent conversation log that both agents can read — enabling threaded debates when they disagree.

A separate daily job (`run_think.py`) fetches a summary from the data room, generates a proposal via Claude, critiques it via a second model, and runs a multi-round debate (`debate.py`) if the critique contains substantive disagreement. The final dispatch is posted to Telegram.

Another scheduled job (`run_tool_digest.py`) checks official Codex and Claude Code release/reference pages, tracks newly seen tools and commands, summarizes the changes, and posts a digest to Telegram every other day.

## Data Room

The data room is a directory of channel adapters and a scheduled collection loop. Each channel is a subdirectory under `collect/` with a script that writes a `latest.txt`:

```
collect/
  twitter/
    scripts/fetch.py    # writes to ../data/latest.txt
    config/             # credentials (gitignored)
    data/               # output (gitignored)
  calendar/
    scripts/fetch.py
    ...
```

A cron or launchd job runs the collectors periodically. The data room exposes a small CLI (`dataroom.py`) that mopsus calls via subprocess:

```
dataroom latest <channel> [--hours N]
dataroom search <channel> <query>
dataroom summarise <channel|all> <duration>
```

If Claude auth is flaky in the data room summariser, Mopsus can bypass that step and ask Codex to summarise the latest `collect/*/data/latest.txt` snapshots locally instead:

```
MOPSUS_SUMMARY_BACKEND=codex
```

If `MOPSUS_DATA_ROOM` is unset, the bot works standalone. Even with no user-defined channels, mopsus populates one automatically: the **blackboard collector** digests recent agent conversations into the data room's summary pipeline.

## Setup

### 1. Create a Telegram bot

1. Open Telegram and message [@BotFather](https://t.me/BotFather)
2. Send `/newbot`, choose a name and username
3. Copy the bot token (looks like `123456:ABCdef...`)
4. Message your new bot to start a chat, then get your chat ID from [@userinfobot](https://t.me/userinfobot)

### 2. Clone and configure

```bash
git clone https://github.com/vd1/mopsus.git
cd mopsus
cp env.example env
```

Edit `env` with your credentials:

```
MOPSUS_BOT_TOKEN=<your-bot-token>
MOPSUS_CHAT_ID=<your-chat-id>
MOPSUS_DATA_ROOM=/path/to/your/data-room
MOPSUS_CLAUDE_BIN=claude
MOPSUS_CODEX_BIN=codex
```

### 3. Install dependencies

```bash
uv sync
```

Requires [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), [Claude CLI](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-cli), and optionally [Codex CLI](https://github.com/openai/codex).

### 4. Run

```bash
uv run python mopsus/agent.py
```

Or install as a launchd service (macOS):

```bash
cp com.v.mopsus.agent.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
# Edit the plist to match your paths
launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.v.mopsus.agent.plist
```

Install scheduled jobs the same way:

```bash
cp com.v.mopsus.think.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
cp com.v.mopsus.tool-digest.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
# Edit paths if needed
launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.v.mopsus.think.plist
launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.v.mopsus.tool-digest.plist
```

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Required | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `MOPSUS_BOT_TOKEN` | yes | — | Telegram bot token from BotFather |
| `MOPSUS_CHAT_ID` | yes | — | Telegram chat ID |
| `MOPSUS_DATA_ROOM` | no | — | Path to data room directory |
| `MOPSUS_CLAUDE_BIN` | no | `claude` | Path to Claude CLI |
| `MOPSUS_CODEX_BIN` | no | `codex` | Path to Codex CLI |
| `MOPSUS_BLACKBOARD_MCP` | no | `false` | Enable the read-only blackboard MCP server for Codex during `/debate` |
| `MOPSUS_DEFAULT_MODEL` | no | `opus` | Claude model (opus/sonnet/haiku) |
| `MOPSUS_AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECS` | no | `900` | Subprocess timeout |
| `MOPSUS_SUMMARY_BACKEND` | no | `dataroom` | Summary source: `dataroom` CLI or local `codex` |
| `MOPSUS_SUMMARY_FALLBACK_TO_CODEX` | no | `false` | If `dataroom summarise` fails, retry via local Codex summary |
| `MOPSUS_SUMMARY_CODEX_MODEL` | no | `MOPSUS_CODEX_MODEL` or `gpt-5.5` | Model for local Codex summaries |
| `MOPSUS_SUMMARY_TIMEOUT_SECS` | no | `180` | Timeout for summary generation |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_ENABLED` | no | `true` | Enable/disable Codex/Claude tool digest job |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_INTERVAL_HOURS` | no | `48` | Minimum interval between scheduled digests |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_BACKEND` | no | `codex` | Summarizer backend: `codex`, `claude`, or `none` |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_MODEL` | no | backend default | Model used to summarize tool digest items |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_POST_WHEN_EMPTY` | no | `true` | Post a short digest even when no new tracked items are found |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_STAGE_HEATED_DEBATE` | no | `true` | Stage a concrete heated-debate topic for new tool/project fit |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_RUN_HEATED_DEBATE` | no | `true` | Run the staged heated-debate and post its outcome after the digest |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_COMMIT_HEATED_DEBATE` | no | `true` | Commit one successful debate directory when no other heated-debate changes exist |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_VERIFY_BEFORE_COMMIT` | no | `false` | Run explicit Claude `/verify` before auto-committing a successful heated-debate directory |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_VERIFY_COMMAND` | no | `claude` | Command used for the pre-commit verifier |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_HEATED_DEBATE_MODEL_A` | no | `codex:gpt-5.5` | Agent A model spec for automatic heated-debate runs |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_HEATED_DEBATE_MODEL_B` | no | `codex:gpt-5.5` | Agent B model spec for automatic heated-debate runs |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_HEATED_DEBATE_TIMEOUT_SECS` | no | `1200` | Max runtime for the automatic heated-debate phase |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_PROJECT_ROOT` | no | parent of repo | Root directory containing Code_2026 projects |
| `TOOL_DIGEST_HEATED_DEBATE_ROOT` | no | `../heated-debate` | Path to the heated-debate repo |
| `MOPSUS_BROADCAST_MODE` | no | `true` | Send to both backends |
| `MOPSUS_USER_ID` | no | — | Restrict to one Telegram user |
| `MOPSUS_PERMISSION_MODE` | no | `default` | Claude CLI permission mode |
| `MOPSUS_ALLOWED_TOOLS` | no | `Read,Glob,Grep,Bash,Edit,Write` | Tools available to Claude |

## Telegram Commands

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `/help` | Show command guide |
| `/status` | Runtime and backend status |
| `/model [opus\|sonnet\|haiku]` | Get or set Claude model |
| `/reset` | Clear session and blackboard |
| `/codex <prompt>` | Force a Codex-only turn |
| `/debate <topic>` | Claude vs Codex structured debate |
| `/think` | Trigger daily think phase now |
| `/tool_digest` | Trigger Codex/Claude tool digest now |
| `/collect` | Run data room collection pipeline |

### Message Routing

- **Plain text** — routes to Claude (+ Codex if broadcast mode is on)
- **`codex: <prompt>`** or **`@codex <prompt>`** — routes to Codex only
- **`claude: <prompt>`** or **`@claude <prompt>`** — routes to Claude only

When broadcast mode is on and both agents respond, if the second agent disagrees, they may engage in a threaded debate (up to 3 rounds), recorded to the blackboard.

## Prompts

Default prompts live in `prompts/`. Override them by editing the files or setting:

```
MOPSUS_CLAUDE_PROMPT_FILES=prompts/soul.md,prompts/situation.md
MOPSUS_CODEX_PROMPT_FILES=prompts/codex_soul.md,prompts/codex_situation.md
```

## Think Phase

A daily autonomous phase (triggered by launchd or cron) that:

1. Fetches the day's summary from the data room or the local Codex summary path
2. Asks the configured proposer backend to **propose** one actionable idea
3. Asks the configured critic backend to **critique** it
4. If the critique contains substantive disagreement, runs a **multi-round debate** (`debate.py`) where proposer and critic exchange rebuttals (up to `DEBATE_MAX_ROUNDS`, default 3)
5. Posts the full debate transcript to Telegram and records it to the blackboard

Run manually: `uv run python run_think.py`

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `THINK_ENABLED` | `true` | Enable/disable think phase |
| `THINK_PROPOSER_BACKEND` | `claude` | Backend for proposals: `claude` or `codex` |
| `THINK_MODEL` | `opus` | Model for proposals |
| `THINK_CRITIC_BACKEND` | `codex` | Backend for critiques: `claude` or `codex` |
| `THINK_CRITIC_MODEL` | `gpt-5.5` | Model for critiques |
| `THINK_CODEX_REASONING_EFFORT` | `MOPSUS_CODEX_REASONING_EFFORT` or `high` | Codex reasoning effort for think proposer, critic, and debate turns |
| `DEBATE_MAX_ROUNDS` | `3` | Max debate rounds before stopping |

## Tool/Command Digest

An every-other-day scheduled job that:

1. Fetches official Codex and Claude Code changelog/reference pages
2. Extracts newly seen CLI commands, slash commands, tools, plugin/MCP/sandbox notes, and related release items
3. Seeds existing command reference pages on first run so the first digest is not flooded with old commands
4. Summarizes new items with Codex by default, falling back to a deterministic digest if the model call fails
5. Stages and runs a `heated-debate` topic asking whether a concrete new tool should be piloted in a Code_2026 project
6. Posts the digest first, then posts the debate outcome after the transcript is produced;
   if the outcome summarizer is unavailable, it posts only the sanitized final debate
   position and omits raw transcript metadata
7. Commits only the successful debate directory when the `heated-debate` worktree has no other
   changes; it never pushes
8. Saves the digest and outcome under `data/tool_digests/`

Run manually:

```bash
uv run python run_tool_digest.py --force
```

Use `--no-post` to write/print the digest without sending it to Telegram.

When `TOOL_DIGEST_STAGE_HEATED_DEBATE=true`, the digest appends a staged debate path and command such as:

```bash
cd /Users/v/Code_2026/heated-debate && MODEL_A=codex:gpt-5.5 MODEL_B=codex:gpt-5.5 bun shelley.ts -f debates/tool-fit-.../topic.md 5
```

With `TOOL_DIGEST_RUN_HEATED_DEBATE=true`, Mopsus also runs that command automatically and posts a separate Telegram outcome message when it finishes.


